BT 1 0 0 1 0 133.4 Tm .225568 Tw 13 TL /F2 9.6 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Summary.) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( A synthetic 90-day e-commerce platform \(10,000 users, 5,000 products, 200,000 sessions with 2.0 M) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.477338 Tw (page views, 50,000 orders worth $53.2 M\) is stored in two NoSQL systems chosen per access pattern -) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.23791 Tw /F2 9.6 Tf (MongoDB) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( for the catalogue, customer profiles and orders \(rich, nested documents\) and ) Tj /F2 9.6 Tf (HBase) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( for the) Tj T* 0 Tw .573011 Tw (clickstream and daily product counters \(append-only, time-ordered, sparse\) - and analysed with ) Tj /F2 9.6 Tf (Apache Spark) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.716775 Tw (which cleans the raw JSON into a Parquet star schema, runs batch analytics and joins the two stores. Key) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.116172 Tw (findings: \(1\) ) Tj /F2 9.6 Tf (38% of sessions flagged 'converted' have no order) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( in the order store; \(2\) ) Tj /F2 9.6 Tf (stock-outs, not) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.01795 Tw (popularity, explain most of the views-to-sales correlation) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( \(r = 0.70 overall, 0.14 for in-stock products\), costing) Tj T* 0 Tw .662972 Tw (~18,600 product views; \(3\) abandoned carts hold ) Tj /F2 9.6 Tf (3.7x the revenue) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( of completed web orders; \(4\) Champions +) Tj T* 0 Tw .247879 Tw (Loyal customers are 52% of buyers but 68% of revenue; \(5\) device, referrer and product co-purchase effects are) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.91677 Tw (statistically indistinguishable from chance - a property of the generator that the analysis detects rather than) Tj T* 0 Tw (over-interprets.) Tj T* ET
