BT 1 0 0 1 0 94.4 Tm 2.056425 Tw 13 TL /F1 9.6 Tf 0 0 0 rg (The generator writes JSON files that feed three paths. ) Tj /F2 9.6 Tf (MongoDB) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( receives categories, products, users and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.390596 Tw (transactions and serves document-shaped questions \(a customer's profile, an order with its lines, revenue by) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.066703 Tw (category\). ) Tj /F2 9.6 Tf (HBase) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( receives every session keyed by user and reverse time plus a daily metric row per product,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.17181 Tw (serving range scans over activity streams and atomic counter updates. ) Tj /F2 9.6 Tf (Spark) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( \(PySpark 3.5\) converts the raw) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.067362 Tw (JSON once into typed Parquet \(job 01\) and runs recommendations, cohorts and Spark SQL on it; the two) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.04477 Tw (integrated queries can read either Parquet \() Tj /F3 9.6 Tf (--source files) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (\) or MongoDB + HBase directly \() Tj /F3 9.6 Tf (--source db) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (\) with) Tj T* 0 Tw .77949 Tw (identical column contracts, so the same analytics code serves both. MongoDB and HBase \(standalone, with its) Tj T* 0 Tw (Thrift server\) are installed by ) Tj /F3 9.6 Tf (setup/setup_ubuntu.sh) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (; the whole pipeline is one command: ) Tj /F3 9.6 Tf (python run_all.py) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (.) Tj T* ET
